  <model metaid="meta_enalapril_liver" id="enalapril_liver" name="Model for hepatic enalapril metabolism." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for the hepatic metabolism of enalapril.</p>
        <p>Enalapril is taken up into the hepatocytes by OATP1B1 (<code>ENAIM</code>) and
hydrolysed by the carboxylesterase 1 (CES1) to its active metabolite
enalaprilat (<code>ENA2EAT</code>), which leaves the hepatocytes slowly (<code>EATEX</code>):
the dicarboxylic acid enalaprilat permeates membranes poorly, enalaprilat
in the plasma peaks 3.5-4.6 hr after an oral dose of enalapril, about
3 hr after enalapril.</p>
        <p>The concentrations of enalapril and enalaprilat in the liver (0.1-6 µM)
are far below the Michaelis constants of the transport and the
conversion (0.4-1.7 mM), so all three are linear and only their ratios
Vmax/Km act.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
